{
  "schema": 2,
  "name": "ft-breakable",
  "title": "Flight test: breakable ship",
  "description": "The flight-test ship among the asteroids, but it can break. Two sliders set how tough it is. Material strength scales every part's damage threshold and toughness: hull parts start at 50 J and 600 J, the tank at 20 J and 100 J. Weld strength scales every weld's limits from the defaults (5 kN tension, 10 kN compression, 3 kN shear, 2 kN·m torque). Turn them down and a hard landing on a rock dents parts, snaps welds and sends legs, nozzles or engines tumbling. A wrecked engine stops firing, and a holed tank leaks its hydrogen and oxygen, which your exhaust can light. Turn them up and the ship bounces off as in FT. The asteroids can't be damaged. Q fires left and E fires right.",
